From 26cfeee9655ed3b501e97b4ec6e3d328cea9d235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:23:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: characterize the RPC client and Tor control behaviour

libevent is about to be replaced in the RPC command line client and the
Tor controller. Record what the libevent implementations do first, so
the replacements can be held to the same behaviour.

- interface_bitcoin_cli_http.py: a raw-socket HTTP server records the
  exact request the CLI sends (request line, header set and order,
  Content-Length, body, the percent-encoded wallet path) and answers
  with scripted responses: chunked and close-delimited bodies, 401 with
  and without credentials, 503, 403, 404/500 JSON errors, empty and
  unparsable bodies, a 50 MB body, a silent server (timeout, error
  code 0), a server that trickles bytes slower than the timeout but
  never pauses for longer (inactivity semantics, succeeds), a refused
  port (libevent reports no error code), a server that closes after
  accepting (error code 1) and a host-name -rpcconnect.
- feature_torcontrol.py: a mock Tor control port drives NULL,
  SAFECOOKIE (including a wrong ServerHash) and HASHEDPASSWORD (quote
  escaping) authentication, ADD_ONION with a new and a cached key, the
  advertised onion address and onion proxy, removal of the address and
  exponential reconnection when the control port goes away, 510
  replies, LF-only and byte-by-byte replies, the host-name parse error
  and the line-length limit (disconnect without reconnecting).
- torcontrol: add ParseTorControlAddress, not yet used, with the forms
  evutil_parse_sockaddr_port accepts. torcontrol_tests checks fixed
  vectors against both it and libevent.
- util_tests: fixed vectors for urlDecode and for libevent's
  evhttp_uriencode, which the client uses for wallet paths.

Tier: eCash
